course: dictionary
lesson: 13363
title: Finding meaning with harmonious
level: primary-5
stars: 0
explain: Harmonious is a describing word. It tells you that things fit together well, so they feel peaceful or pleasant. You can meet it between people, in music and in art. «The harmonious class worked together without a single argument.» The clue is without an argument, so harmonious means friendly and peaceful.
explain: In music, harmonious describes notes that sound pleasant when they are played or sung together. «The choir's harmonious singing filled the hall.» The clue is singing, so think of sounds that blend nicely. In art, it describes colours that look good side by side. «The painting had harmonious blues and greens.»
explain: Read the words around the word first, then swap your meaning into the sentence to check it. Does a harmonious class get along well? Yes, so your meaning fits and you can trust it.
fact: Harmonious means friendly and peaceful, without arguments.
fact: In music, harmonious means having notes that sound pleasant together.
fact: For colours or things, harmonious means fitting together nicely.
fact: Harmonious comes from harmony, which is when things fit together well.
fact: «The garden looked harmonious, with pink roses and soft green leaves.»
exercise: «The harmonious class worked together without a single argument.» What does harmonious mean here? | *Friendly and peaceful | Late and tired | Loud and noisy | Very hungry
exercise: «The choir's harmonious singing filled the hall.» What does harmonious mean here? | Covered in paint | Sad and slow | *Having notes that sound pleasant together | Very fast and loud
exercise: Which example shows harmonious colours? | Muddy brown with no other shades | Black ink spilled on white paper | *Blue and green that look good together | A bright red spot on a grey sheet
test: «The harmonious team shared the work fairly.» What does harmonious suggest? | Loud and rude | Unhappy and angry | Lost and confused | *Friendly and peaceful
test: Which sentence uses harmonious correctly? | Harmonious is a kind of food | The harmonious dog barked all night | I harmonious my bike | *The family had a harmonious evening with no fights
exam: Ruby says harmonious means noisy. Who is right? | *You, because harmonious means peaceful and pleasant | Ruby, because harmonious means loud | Nobody, the word has no meaning | Both, it means noisy and peaceful
